{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/tsconfig",
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "noEmit": true,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false,
    // Vite's config and Playwright's config live next to `src/`, not under it — the base
    // `rootDir: "src"` would put both outside the program and fail with TS6059. `apps/api` never
    // needed this override because it has no config files of its own inside its tsconfig's scope.
    "rootDir": ".",
    "types": ["node", "vite/client"],
    // `baseUrl` is what makes dependency-cruiser resolve `@/*` at all. `tsc` itself does not need
    // it — TypeScript's own `paths` resolution has worked baseUrl-less since 4.1 — but
    // dependency-cruiser's `normalize.mjs` only lets `tsconfig-paths-webpack-plugin` use this
    // file's own directory as its base when `ts.parseJsonConfigFileContent` reports a `baseUrl`;
    // absent one, it forces the plugin's base to the cruise's CWD (the repo root) instead, so
    // `@/lib/x` was looked up as `<repo-root>/src/lib/x` and silently failed to resolve
    // (docs/open-questions.md, row dated 24/08/2026). `ignoreDeprecations` is TS's own prescribed
    // escape for TS5101 ("baseUrl... will stop functioning in TypeScript 7.0"): this repository
    // pins `typescript@6.0.3` exactly, so the deprecation is live today. **Revisit at the next
    // TypeScript bump**: either dependency-cruiser has caught up to baseUrl-less `paths` by then,
    // or this option and its comment need replacing with whatever TS 7 requires instead.
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "ignoreDeprecations": "6.0",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": [
    "src/**/*.ts",
    "src/**/*.tsx",
    "e2e/**/*.spec.ts",
    "vite.config.ts",
    "playwright.config.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "coverage"]
}
